\f1  Setting Up Python and the Right Tools\
\
We need Python 3.10 or higher and a tool called uv, which is a fast package manager for Python.\
\
Step 1: Install uv\

\f0 \uc0\u55357 \u56633 
\f1  Mac/Linux:\
\
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh  \

\f0 \uc0\u55357 \u56633 
\f1  Windows: Follow the instructions at uv\'92s installation page.\
\
After installation, restart your terminal so uv is recognized.\
\
Step 2: Set Up a Virtual Environment\
uv venv  \
source .venv/bin/activate  # Mac/Linux  \
or  \
.venv\\Scripts\\activate     # Windows  \
\
Step 3: Install CREWAI\
uv tool install crewai\
\
Step 4: Verify Installation \
uv tool list\
\
Step5: Make sure to setup AZ CLI\
\
Step6: Login using AZ login command\

